  "id": "54eaff2d-e7da-46ed-a01e-026de57bdd10",
  "message": "The compaction happens in the Lance DB‑based shared‑memory table, not inside any of the language models. When the mechanic runs a compact‑and‑restart, it clears out the entries stored in that Lance DB store, so any persisted facts are removed. The LLMs (Letta, Claude, etc.) don’t hold that long‑term memory themselves, so they don’t compact anything—they simply read from or write to the database. In short, the database is what’s compacted, and no model is responsible for that step.",
